>> title: Bolognese
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: beef, pork, tomato, pasta, stovetop
>> counters: Pizzeria
>> aka: ragù alla bolognese, ragu, meat sauce, spaghetti bolognese
>> pairs-with: bechamel
>> servings: 8
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: forgiving — three hours or four and the sauce only gets rounder, and it is better the next day and freezes well; the milk and the wine each have to be reduced until the pan is nearly dry before the next goes in, and a pot rushed there stays thin for the whole three hours
>> step.1: sweat 12 min
>> step.2: brown 15 min
>> step.3: reduce until dry
>> step.4: reduce until dry
>> step.5: simmer 3 hr

Sweat @pancetta{3%oz}(85 g; finely chopped), @yellow onion{1%medium}(finely diced), @carrot{1%medium}(finely diced), and @celery{1%rib}(finely diced) in @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(45 g) over medium heat for ~{12%min}.

Brown @ground beef chuck{1%lb}(450 g) and @ground pork{1/2%lb}(225 g) in @&(~1)soffritto{} with @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} for ~{15%min}, breaking up the meat.

Reduce @whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL) and @grated nutmeg{1/8%tsp} into @&(~1)meat{} until the pan is nearly dry.

Reduce @dry white wine{1%cup}(240 mL) into @&(~1)meat{} until the pan is nearly dry.

Simmer @&(~1)meat{} with @canned whole tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g; crushed) at the barest bubble for ~{3%hr}.
